id: pm-gh1593
title: "GH-1593: verify authoritative history integrity in SDK mutation-event reads"
description: "## Observed\n\n`listMutationEvents` (and other reads served from the runtime history-event index) keep returning events from the cache after the authoritative history file was modified, as long as the file length is unchanged. Nothing in the result tells the caller the cache and the source disagree.\n\nMinimal reproduction on `@unbrained/pm-cli` **2026.10.25** (fresh install in a temp project, non-git tracker):\n\n1. `pm init`, then create one item.\n2. Prime the index: `listMutationEvents({ full: true })` through the SDK.\n3. In `.agents/pm/history/<id>.jsonl`, flip one hex character of a `record_hash` without changing the file length.\n4. Call `listMutationEvents({ full: true })` again, both in the same process and after a restart.\n\n**Result:** the cached chain is returned and verifies. `verifyHistoryEntries` on the authoritative file fails. The read response carries no integrity or completeness receipt that would reveal the disagreement.\n\n## Impact\n\nPackages that recover or act on mutation events (notification outboxes, sync cursors, closeout bots) read corrupted or tampered history as healthy unless they re-verify the raw files themselves. Measured in the pm fleet on 2026-10-25: three packages (pm-slack, pm-rlm, pm-todos) had to add their own raw `verifyHistoryEntries` pass after adopting the SDK event API. A review found that pm-slack queued notifications with `failed: 0` for a corrupted history.\n\n## Expected\n\n- **Cache validity:** keyed by content, not just length or mtime. For example, store a digest of each history file (or of its last record hash) and compare it before serving; a cheap prefix/last-record check is enough to catch rewritten records.\n- **Integrity receipt:** event reads return a receipt such as `integrity: \"verified\" | \"cache_unverified\" | \"mismatch\"`. Callers that act on events can then require `verified`, or ask the SDK to verify the affected items' authoritative chains.\n- **Strict option:** a documented `verify: true` option for event reads that verifies the authoritative chain of every returned item, so packages stop re-implementing it.\n\nRelated: #1485 (index lock contention), #1585 (side effects of refused mutations).\n"
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: "gh:1593",history,integrity,sdk
