claim_principal: "harness:codex#9a3d0027739dfadbcc41b040"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Same-length history rewrites invalidate cached event results; SDK event readers expose explicit integrity semantics and a strict authoritative-chain verification option; Existing non-Git connector consumers can use the public contract without raw-path verification; Positive and corrupted-history controls cover process-local and restarted index reads; Cache verification covers the complete authoritative stream and detects same-length non-tail record edits even when the final record and hash remain unchanged
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: high
confidence: 85
expected_result: Content receipts use the exact original history bytes; unverified full entries remain stable across prior strict reads; selected complete chains fail closed on corruption and content validation bounds concurrent reads.
